# SAFE BEST PRACTICES
{"instruction": "shell script best practices", "output": "**Safe Shell Scripting Practices**\n\n**1. Always Validate Input:**\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n\n# Check arguments\nif [ -z \"$1\" ]; then\n    echo \"Error: No argument provided\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\n# Validate path is safe\nif [[ \"$1\" == /* ]]; then\n    echo \"Error: Absolute paths not allowed\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n**2. Use Quotes:**\n```bash\n# Dangerous\nrm $filename\n\n# Safe\nrm \"$filename\"\n```\n\n**3. Set Safety Options:**\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -euo pipefail  # Exit on error, undefined vars, pipe failures\n```\n\n**4. Check Before Destructive Operations:**\n```bash\nif [ -f \"$file\" ]; then\n    echo \"Warning: $file exists. Overwrite? (y/n)\"\n    read answer\n    if [ \"$answer\" != \"y\" ]; then\n        exit 0\n    fi\nfi\n```\n\n**5. Avoid Dangerous Commands:**\n```bash\n# ❌ NEVER do this\nrm -rf /$variable  # If $variable is empty = disaster!\n\n# ✅ Safe approach\nif [ -n \"$variable\" ] && [ -d \"$variable\" ]; then\n    rm -rf \"$variable\"\nfi\n```\n\n**6. Log Actions:**\n```bash\nLOGFILE=\"~/operation.log\"\necho \"[$(date)] Starting operation\" >> \"$LOGFILE\"\n```\n\n**7. Use Functions:**\n```bash\nsafe_delete() {\n    local file=\"$1\"\n    if [ -f \"$file\" ]; then\n        mv \"$file\" \"$file.backup\"\n        echo \"✓ Backup created\"\n    fi\n}\n```\n\n🛡️ **Safety Checklist:**\n✓ Validate all inputs\n✓ Quote variables\n✓ Check file existence\n✓ Create backups\n✓ Test with dummy data\n✓ Use -i flag for rm/mv\n✓ Log operations"}

